Single-database Alembic environment for the Executor PostgreSQL schema.

Revision `0001` is the complete pre-release schema baseline recorded on 2026-08-19. It replaces
the former incremental development chain and is intended to create a new empty database directly
at the current schema. Existing databases stamped with a removed development revision must be
recreated; no compatibility or data-preserving upgrade path is provided for that discarded chain.
Revision `0002` is the current head. It adds monotonic fencing tokens to Execution and Attempt
ownership so an expired Worker cannot mutate durable state after a later claim.

Create or verify a database with:

    uv run alembic upgrade head
    uv run alembic current
    uv run alembic check

Service startup never runs Alembic automatically. Run it as a release/init job before starting
Executor processes.
